sam: Heads-up: ZenithCare POC needs a one-pager for devs. They want ephemeral handshake, streaming knobs for backpressure, how tool/function calls work, and how we enforce structured JSON outputs. Also a quick cost hint for ~40 req/s @ ~1k tokens avg. Can someone craft a tiny copy/paste runbook?
priya: Hosted POC to start. Keep it simple. Include a curl for ephemeral token, minimal WS handshake, a small Node snippet for tool_response, and a note about schema validation.
tom: Quick checklist I use: 1) request ephemeral token from presales endpoint; 2) plug token into SDK credentialProvider; 3) open stream with subprotocol `rwd-stream-v1`; 4) send `meta` frame with `schema_id` (and `strict:true` if you want validation); 5) listen for `toolcall` and reply with `tool_response`; 6) enable client-side inflight limit and heartbeat.
priya: Streaming knobs suggestion: max_inflight=5, heartbeat=20s, retry backoff on 429 with jitter (base 150ms). If they expect bursts, advise batching via REST endpoints instead of long-lived high-concurrency streams.
tom: Minimal curl for ephemeral token (presales env):
```bash
curl -s -X POST https://presales.redwood.ai/v1/ephemeral
  -H "Authorization: Bearer PRESALES_KEY"
  -H "Content-Type: application/json"
  -d '{"account":"zenithcare","purpose":"poc"}'
# returns: {"token":"ey...","expires_in":900}
```
sam: Node snippet I can paste into their repo?
priya: Pasteable Node example: 
```js
const client = new RedwoodClient({ credentialProvider: async () => ({ token: await getEphemeral() }), streaming: true });
const stream = await client.stream({ model: 'rwd-4-small', multiplex: true });
// send schema upfront
stream.send({ type: 'meta', schema_id: 'zenithcare-v1', strict: true });
stream.on('message', async (msg) => {
  if (msg.type === 'toolcall') {
    const res = await callExternalService(msg.args);
    stream.send({ type: 'tool_response', id: msg.id, result: res });
  }
  if (msg.type === 'chunk') { /* accumulate tokens */ }
});
```
finance-bot: Pricing hint: 40 rps * 1k tokens ≈ 3.5B tokens/day if run 24/7; for typical business-hours POC (8h/day) it's ~1.2B tokens. Hosted cost for a short POC is usually a few thousand USD depending on model and caching. Recommend a 1-2 hour representative run to get an accurate estimate; we can offer a short Dedicated trial if they need sustained high throughput.
sam: Can you also add a one-paragraph runbook I can paste into my onboarding email?
priya: One-paragraph runbook (copy/paste): "Request an ephemeral token from our presales endpoint using your account id, then use that token with the Redwood SDK credentialProvider to open a WebSocket to wss://stream.redwood.ai/v1?model=<model> with subprotocol `rwd-stream-v1`. Send a `meta` JSON frame with `schema_id` (and `strict:true` to enable server-side schema validation), stream inputs, and handle `toolcall` messages by replying with `tool_response` frames. For high throughput use short batch REST calls or request a Dedicated trial. Example handshake curl: `curl -X POST https://presales.redwood.ai/v1/ephemeral -H 'Authorization: Bearer PRESALES_KEY' -d '{"account":"zenithcare"}'`."
tom: I'll upload a tiny demo repo and ping finance for a more precise quote.
priya: ops-bot: presales/runbooks deployed (files: zenithcare-runbook.md, node-examples.js) :white_check_mark:
sam: Great — I'll send to the customer and set a follow-up demo. Thanks! :thumbsup:
